Ideas (no text copied)
- Felix Rieseberg, "How to Be More Ambitious: A Tutorial for Humans with Models" (2026-10-13):
  the altitude / depth / range framing. All wording in this skill is original.
- Anthropic and OpenAI public prompting guides: contract elements (done criteria, stop rules,
  reasons behind constraints), long-context placement.

Adapted from MIT-licensed projects (method and short phrasing adapted, rewritten)
- Matt Pocock, `grilling` skill (MIT): interviewing in rounds over the frontier of a decision tree.
- nidhinjs/prompt-master (MIT) https://github.com/nidhinjs/prompt-master
  input sanitization; no framework names in the output.
- ckelsoe/prompt-architect (MIT) https://github.com/ckelsoe/prompt-architect
  visible placeholders instead of invented facts; never drop a prohibition.
- k-vaca/prompt-engineering-skill (MIT) https://github.com/k-vaca/prompt-engineering-skill
  gold input/output pairs as the definition of done; edge behavior; reasoning vs non-reasoning
  targets; untrusted input treated as data.
- openai/openai-cookbook (MIT) https://github.com/openai/openai-cookbook
  checking that examples obey the prompt's rules.
- gsd-build/get-shit-done (MIT) https://github.com/gsd-build/get-shit-done
  stating inferred facts as assumptions with evidence instead of asking.
- CR-730/agent-system-prompt-architect-skill (MIT)
  https://github.com/CR-730/agent-system-prompt-architect-skill
  keeping pipeline vocabulary out of the emitted prompt.
- anthropics/claude-cookbooks metaprompt (MIT) https://github.com/anthropics/claude-cookbooks
  data first, question last; reasoning before the verdict.

